[{"id":4890763266,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI4MgAg","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`current_bone < 0 || root_bone < 0` means that bones are not set. Therefore, I judge that checking if the bone index exceeds the size here is not the right place.\n\nThe correct way to fix would be to initialize the bone specification when a non-existent bone is found within `SkeletonModifier3D::_validate_bone_names()` and set its index to `-1`. This should prevent moving to subsequent lines due to the `current_bone < 0 || root_bone < 0` check.\n\nBTW, I think this issue exists in other places besides SpringBoneSimulator3D as well, so it would be ideal if consistent handling could be applied to all of them.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122053#pullrequestreview-4890763266","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122053","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/1